WEBVTT

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:16.570
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:27.590
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but reality moves on.</i>

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:33.120
<i>Treat love as love, treat</i>
<i>dreams as dreams.</i>

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:38.630
<i>It's difficult to say it in earnest.</i>
<i>The times forge ahead, but...</i>

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:43.540
<i>I want to make you happy...</i>

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:49.330
<i>I'll do so like I do to</i>
<i>be myself. Yeah!</i>

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.370
<i>I'll make you happy...</i>

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:59.780
<i>I dedicate all that</i>
<i>I can do to you.</i>

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:11.100
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:23.340
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but love doesn't stop for me.</i>

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:28.910
This place?

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:30.400
This is it!

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:33.450
Hello!

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:38.510
Hi! Thanks for coming!

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:39.490
Hi!

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.390
Congratulations on your move,
and your new shop!

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.300
Thank you.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.500
"Grand Opening"
Thank you.
Where's Dad?

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.490
He's in the back, sorting inventory.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.430
He sure caught me
off-guard this time.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:54.030
I didn't really think he was going
to open up a motorcycle shop.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:02:00.740
Daimaru always wanted to open a shop
here in Tokyo, close to you.

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:04.140
Here you are. Help yourself
to some tea.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:05.250
Thank you.

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:07.280
Natsumi's coming along
too, isn't she?

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:09.420
Yes, she's supposed to be.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:12.180
She should be here soon,
don't you think?

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:24.500
FILE. l9
THE 8ROKEN DREAM
OF A 8IKE MECHANIC

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:35.210
Great time for a clutch
cable to snap.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:40.850
I shouldn't have ridden
the coast road.

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:45.280
I wonder if there's a motorbike repair
shop around here somewhere...

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:51.820
I heard at the station flower stand that
this shop is quite the attraction.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.430
Uh... yeah.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:54.930
What's the matter?

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.940
Well... we do get customers, but...

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:58.670
Hello?

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.660
Speak of the devil!
Hello?

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.170
H... Hello!

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:05.070
Can I help
you?

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:06.110
See what I mean?

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:08.240
Yeah, what a babe!

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.380
What is it you're looking for?

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.080
Well, uh...

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:15.420
I'll call my husband and
ask him to help you.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.380
Darling!

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:19.490
Hey... Did she say her?

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:20.650
Maybe we should...

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.730
Hello! What can
I do for you?

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:26.930
What the!

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:30.260
This geezer's her husband?!

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.270
D'uh... Gotta go!

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.570
Thanks very much!

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:43.610
How odd! That's been
going on all morning!

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:46.380
What in the world
is going on?

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:49.210
I think I'm starting
to get the picture.

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:50.550
Yeah.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:53.190
"KANNO AUTO"
"Motorcycle Sales & Repairs"

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:55.750
Hey! Lucky me!

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:56.290
"Kanno Auto"

00:03:56.290 --> 00:04:01.830
I knew things would
go my way. Hi?!

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:04.900
Cheers!

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.160
Well!

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:08.910
Drink and eat up!

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.430
This pizza is delicious!

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:12.510
It really is!

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:15.450
You think so? I made it myself.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:15.780
Is it good? Do you like it? Do you?!

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:20.270
Ow! Hey! Let me go! That hurts!

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:22.490
Is it all right leaving the shop like that?

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:25.150
Sure. We have to celebrate, after all.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.690
I see.

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:30.960
What is it?

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:33.360
This is really awesome.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.690
Getting together
like this.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.240
Like a family, sitting around the table.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:40.570
Family?

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:42.330
What's gotten into you?!

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:44.910
That's ridiculous.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.680
It's not crazy! We're family, a happy family!

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:51.080
Hey! You're choking me! Stop it! Hey!

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:52.180
Boy!

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.650
Umm... Hello?

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.290
Hello!

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:06.160
Anybody here?

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:17.400
Hey, you. Looking for
something here?

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.210
U... Uh...

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:21.010
...my clutch cable
snapped.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.610
I don't work
here.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:25.910
Sorry, I didn't
realize.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:29.420
You're not from around
here, are you?

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.710
Uh, doesn't look like this place
is open today, does it?

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:37.160
That old man always
leaves it like this.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:40.230
Hardly ever shows up.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:43.030
He runs it by himself.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:48.360
He's getting old, and he's not
as spry as he used to be.

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:51.230
Is that right?

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:53.440
Well, that won't help me.

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:59.750
"Kuwabara;" chant similarto "God, save me."
Kuwabara! Kuwabara!

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:10.550
Need something fixed?

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:12.280
Yes.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:18.830
Let's have a
look at it.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.740
Nice work.

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:28.670
Huh?

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:32.340
Good methodical work.
Good power.

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:35.850
Uh, actually the clutch
cable is broken.

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:38.220
Are you the one
who did it?

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:43.220
Yeah, I was riding the coast
road, when it just snapped.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.150
That's not what
I mean.

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:48.720
I'm asking if you're the
one who tuned it up.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:52.260
Oh. No, not me.

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:01.500
The cable and the tools
are over there.

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:05.480
But I've never done
this before!

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:10.420
It just won't do.

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:12.650
What? Uh...

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:15.190
You're not qualified
to ride this bike.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:17.820
Come again, real soon.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.960
Hey! Wait a minute!

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:27.260
Here...

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:28.110
...Natsumi.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:30.010
"Summer Flavor"

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:30.780
Thanks.

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:33.770
We were all worried
about you.

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:36.400
You should have seen Sena.
Because you were coming...

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:38.850
...she cooked enough
food for 5 people.

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:44.860
And Daimaru and Nakajima ended
up drunk and passed out.

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:49.960
Give me back my
food! Dammit.

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:56.270
So, did you leave
your bike there?

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:59.230
Sounds like a weird
mechanic.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:02.770
I'm going back for it
on my next day off.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:06.270
Argh! My beautiful RZ!

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:08.210
This is a good
opportunity...

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:10.280
...so, how about you learn
a little bit about it?

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:12.380
Give me
a break!

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:16.250
Even if he was able to tell how
good your tuning skills are...

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.590
He's not doing
his job!

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:22.120
I'm going to get it back
if it kills me.

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:25.660
Hmm... Kanno
Auto, huh?

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:37.040
You're back.

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:40.040
Put those on. I'll show
you the ropes.

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:49.810
What the hell am I doing here, anyway?
This is getting downright weird.

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:52.120
Mister?

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:53.450
Good.

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:55.550
Then let's start.

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:59.060
That's right. It's the reverse
of when you took it off.

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:01.360
My one day off!

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:04.300
No, not there! How many times
do I have to tell you?!

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:05.870
Right about now
I should be...

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:08.700
It just won't do.

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:13.940
That's a homer!

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:21.580
Konoyono-Hayate is closing in
on the leading horses, folks!

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:24.090
The race is getting close as they
round the second corner...

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:26.660
Looks like it's going to
be one dramatic finale!

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:30.020
Leaving the last horse, Nohintojitsu,
all 11 horses are...

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:33.600
Hey!

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:34.320
I did it!

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:38.170
Really?

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:40.170
Then you've gotten to
know your bike...

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:42.360
...a little better
than before.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:45.940
Does that mean I can
take it home now?

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:51.050
No. Check the brake fluid, the chain,
and change the transmission fluid.

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:51.770
Huh?

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:04.620
It's not the kind of thing
you can rush.

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:06.920
You've got to be careful
and precise.

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:10.020
A machine has life.

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:13.260
And anyone who can't fix his own ma-
chine doesn't deserve to ride it!

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:20.640
Listen.

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:24.770
To give your bike a tune-up
is to develop its potential.

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:30.120
The rider becomes one with the
bike, and they evolve together.

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:34.880
Their lives intertwined, they
ride through time together.

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:46.930
Hey, you did a pretty
good job, Natsumi!

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:48.660
Of course.

00:10:48.770 --> 00:10:52.640
I had to endure all the old man's bitching
before he'd give it back.

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:55.750
Still, it's hard to believe you got
all this done in just one day.

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:57.680
You should be grateful!

00:10:58.250 --> 00:11:02.650
Well, it is true that I'm unbelievably
better at this now!

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:03.490
Hey!

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:07.360
Hey!
I didn't mean that I'm better than Miyuki!

00:11:07.530 --> 00:11:08.320
Of course not!

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.860
That old man's just a good
teacher, that's all.

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:15.360
Come to think of it, he sure
knows how to use people.

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:17.470
The old man didn't even lift a finger.

00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:19.100
The old man didn't even lift a finger.
Natsumi?

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:21.530
Were you the one who
tuned the carburetor?

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:23.540
Uh-uh. Didn't touch it.

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:25.530
Uh-uh. Didn't touch it.
So the old man did?

00:11:25.710 --> 00:11:27.380
Um... yeah... I guess so.

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:29.110
Um... yeah... I guess so.
I see.

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:36.580
What's the
matter?

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:39.320
Tsujimoto!

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:40.590
What is it?

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:41.760
Come here.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.130
What?

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:44.260
This is awful!

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:45.230
What is?

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:47.600
She's furious!

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:48.430
How come?

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:50.130
She's in shock.

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:50.830
But why?!

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:54.030
It's that great
tune-up!

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:59.300
How would you feel if some old man you'd
never met fiddled with your work?

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:03.810
And especially if he's more
skilled than she is...

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:04.480
Then she'd be really upset!

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:06.070
Exactly!

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:09.520
She's got pride,
you know!

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:12.950
And now you've gone and stuck
the last dagger in her back!

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:15.920
I beg your pardon?! Are
you blaming me?!

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:16.820
Huh?

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:21.900
Lucky you.

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:25.960
You've really been taken
good care of.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:29.330
See? You've got it
all wrong again!

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:40.650
Hi, Pops!

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:42.810
You again.

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:45.580
You don't need anything
from me. Go home.

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:48.030
But I've come all this way to see you!

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:48.990
Cut that out!

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:51.250
You're just shy!

00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:52.050
Leave me alone.

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:54.770
I brought my partner along with me today.

00:12:54.770 --> 00:12:55.560
Who's that?

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:58.170
The person who's been tuning
up my bike all this time.

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:01.300
Your partner did that?

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:05.510
Anyway, I said I'd introduce
her. Just a second...

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:06.580
Huh?

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.840
That's strange...

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:10.540
It just won't do.

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:17.280
Most of these parts are
for racing bikes.

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:28.330
Huh?! What's
this picture?

00:13:32.570 --> 00:13:35.370
It's the same one
as Daimaru's.

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:44.370
Look what I found!

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:50.440
This is a motorbike, isn't it?! And I bet
it's not an average one, either!

00:13:50.620 --> 00:13:51.650
Stop it!

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:54.820
Keep your hands
off that!

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:03.960
Cool!

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:05.120
Listen!

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:07.030
Don't touch it! You
can't touch it!

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:08.900
You've got to keep
your hands off it!

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:10.270
Mr. Kanno?

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:12.710
It's a Ducati L-Twin!

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:15.700
Who would've guessed
I'd see it here!

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:18.240
Where've you been?!

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:20.890
Are you her partner?

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:22.440
Yes, I'm Miyuki Kobayakawa.

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:26.420
You're the mechanic who was famous
throughout Japan ten years ago...

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:27.860
...Takaya Kanno, right?

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:29.320
What?! You know him?

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:33.620
A Ducati. You were the best at
tuning up Ducati L-Twins...

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:35.220
...and it's told that anyone
who rode one of those...

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:38.300
...felt as if they were
under a magic spell.

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:39.770
Wow!

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:40.760
They even said...

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:43.430
...that the machines couldn't
withstand your skill.

00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:46.240
But you retired after
only two years...

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:48.830
...because of
an accident.

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:51.140
H... How do you
know all that?

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:57.610
That was all a long,
long time ago.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:59.810
"It just won't do."

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:04.690
That's what you always used
to say. Right, Taka?

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:05.790
It's you!

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:07.660
Nakajima!

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:12.630
I heard about a strange bike shop, and
I had to come check it out for myself.

00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:18.770
It's been over
10 years...

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:20.870
Despite the fact that we
were middle-aged...

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.810
...we were trying to break
the speed record.

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:32.190
<i>"Nakajima...</i>

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:33.880
<i>"...it's no good!"</i>

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:36.350
<i>"We should pull out."</i>

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:38.220
<i>"I know everything</i>
<i>about this bike!"</i>

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:39.260
<i>"It's good as it is."</i>

00:15:39.260 --> 00:15:41.230
<i>"It's good as it is."</i>
<i>"Yeah, but..."</i>

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:52.610
<i>"What speed! In 2nd place, number3</i>
<i>Daimaru Nakajima and his Ducati!"</i>

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:55.180
<i>"It's the last lap</i>
<i>of the GP 500."</i>

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:57.680
<i>"Nakajima closes in!"</i>

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:00.320
<i>"Don't push it,</i>
<i>Nakajima!"</i>

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:11.930
We were ahead.

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:14.790
We were sure we were
going to win.

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:18.830
Our passion for the race
was unrelenting.

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:22.370
Then the final lap, where
it's all-or-nothing...

00:16:22.470 --> 00:16:25.570
...we were one lap away from
realizing our dream.

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:45.730
<i>"Nakajima!"</i>

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:49.330
We pushed too far!

00:16:49.430 --> 00:16:52.200
We pushed the engine
beyond its limit...

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:55.270
...knocking the bike
out of balance.

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:02.740
We were so passionate
that day.

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:05.780
Fortune was
on our side.

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:07.310
But, then in the
last turn...

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:12.750
...it turned away
from us.

00:17:13.820 --> 00:17:18.260
It wasn't your fault. I was the one
who didn't follow your advice.

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:22.300
No. I tuned up
the bike.

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:23.960
Because of
this bike...

00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:26.730
...you lost the sight
in your left eye.

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:29.770
And I wrecked my leg
in a drunken binge.

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:34.740
We old-timers are
over the hill.

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:37.350
Mr. Kanno!

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:44.020
Our dreams ended at that last
corner... with the crash.

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:46.590
It just won't do.

00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:57.360
Yeah, it just
won't do!

00:17:58.170 --> 00:17:59.800
I told you, don't
touch that!

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:03.740
Quit grumbling, and
let's go for it!

00:18:04.010 --> 00:18:07.440
From the last corner,
to the finish line!

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:10.410
Come on! We're
all here for you!

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:13.150
She just won't quit.

00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:31.630
Hey, you ready?

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:35.460
You bet! Let's
go, Natsumi!

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:36.310
Okay.

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:37.860
Okay.
Let's do it!

00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:53.190
Yo! Taka!

00:18:56.330 --> 00:18:57.730
Why, this is...

00:18:57.830 --> 00:18:59.460
This is the
same!

00:18:59.630 --> 00:19:01.690
I've been saving
it all along...

00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:04.070
...for this very occasion.

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:11.700
In the dry night...

00:19:11.810 --> 00:19:16.610
<i>... your voice is coming back...</i>

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:21.990
<i>... slowly...</i>

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:23.650
Everything will be all right.
<i>... slowly...</i>

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:23.720
<i>... slowly...</i>

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:26.690
Natsumi'll be able to handle that bike!
<i>... slowly...</i>

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:30.060
<i>... rusty.</i>
That's right.

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:30.130
<i>... rusty.</i>

00:19:30.130 --> 00:19:32.400
That super machine...
<i>... rusty.</i>

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:32.460
<i>... rusty.</i>

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:35.100
...was tuned by two top mechanics,
both young and old.

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:35.270
<i>... rusty.</i>

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:38.130
It won't easily fail us.

00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:43.640
<i>The moon is crying out...</i>

00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:44.740
Don't push it.

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:54.140
<i>... holding the frigid Ioneliness..</i>

00:19:55.050 --> 00:20:03.790
<i>... holding the freezing heartbeat.</i>

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:14.600
<i>I want to sleep in your arms...</i>

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:17.740
<i>The dream named love has disappeared...</i>

00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:19.810
You can never stop dreaming.

00:20:19.810 --> 00:20:20.380
<i>The dream named love has disappeared...</i>

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:22.880
I'll show you how a dream begins!

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:22.950
<i>The dream named love has disappeared...</i>

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:26.850
Your dream's going to come true!

00:20:27.050 --> 00:20:38.260
<i>Where should I keep running?</i>

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:43.460
<i>To the dawn...</i>

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:14.630
All right!
Hurray!

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:25.070
Ha! It just
won't do.

00:22:06.850 --> 00:22:12.420
<i>I live my life my own way, doing</i>
<i>things others wouldn't.</i>

00:22:12.690 --> 00:22:21.030
<i>Being strong isn't enough.</i>
<i>It makes me Ionely.</i>

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:32.040
<i>I can feel your presence</i>
<i>as if you're right here...</i>

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:40.080
<i>... but I can't say a word.</i>

00:22:41.620 --> 00:22:48.880
<i>The feelings I hide within might</i>
<i>break into pieces...</i>

00:22:50.430 --> 00:22:57.800
<i>But if I don't say anything,</i>
<i>nothing can begin.</i>

00:22:58.140 --> 00:23:05.360
<i>The wind gently blows...</i>
<i>Time flows...</i>

00:23:05.540 --> 00:23:15.090
<i>Time flows... And soon</i>
<i>I can be honest...</i>

00:23:15.220 --> 00:23:18.180
<i>Thank you,</i>
<i>friend!</i>

